_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` while the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I'll check the test's expected values against half-even: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 (7 is odd, so round up to 8) and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 (6 is even, so stay). Both match. Next I'll create the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VSyxS96YHz4cCidt59bx9c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BtjnwgadybFjMiWwwoZ9VD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed to the branch. Next I'll start CI on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01C5g1WFLEG7mdzve2X8ZRNv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fix-banker-rounding-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WJMLfVyHC36AovzUPiGq5C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01B5gUczeXpqYJD5tgSMatYj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Nightly build fails because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChange: `round_money` now quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, matching the docstring and FIN-212.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986 (tests/test_money.py, including 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-banker-rounding-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer. I did not merge it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and the docstring call for banker's rounding.\n- **Fix:** Switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`). I checked the test's expected values against half-even: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101, titled \"Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212\".", "type": "text"}]}]}